+/*
+ * SWEET vayu (SM8150): modem (MPSS) bring-up, milestone 1 - the modem is loaded, authenticated and let
+ * out of reset, the link to it taken up, and the application processor's file services started, so that
+ * the modem can register its services (WLFW among them: the Wi-Fi firmware service this is all for).
+ * After HakiOS hakios.mpss.c (oosexgang/hackios-xnu-kernel, APSL 2.0), with the numbers of this SoC and
+ * its one architectural difference: vayu has no IPCC. Where HakiOS rings a doorbell through IPCC and
+ * reads IPCC for the modem's rings, here outgoing doorbells are single-bit writes to the APCS register
+ * 0x17c0000c (AOP bit 0, GLINK bit 12, SMP2P bit 14) and there is no incoming-doorbell register at all:
+ * the modem's SPI interrupts (GLINK 449, SMP2P 451) are not taken, the shared memory and the GLINK
+ * queues are polled instead (a thread of ours, every millisecond).
+ *
+ *   vayu DT, from iOS/modem.md:
+ *   - qcom,mss@4080000: pil-tz-generic, pas-id 4, no MBA; modem_region 0x8e000000 + 0x9600000
+ *   - reserved-memory smem 0x86000000 + 0x200000; hwlock@1f40000, lock 3 at 0x1f43000, apps value 1
+ *   - qcom,smp2p-modem: qcom,smem <435 428> (435 the modem's, 428 ours), hosts apps 0 / modem 1
+ *   - qcom,glink/modem: IPCRTR, SMEM items 478 (descriptor) 479 (our queue) 480 (the modem's)
+ *   - crash reason item 421; AOP mailbox qcom,qmp-aop@c300000
+ *   - rails cx.lvl and mss.lvl at level 385 while it boots (sweet_rpmh.c: sweet_rpmh_arc_vote)
+ *   - rmtfs 3 MB, TrustZone HLOS (3) + MSS_MSA (15) only (no NAV); its buffer put at a free no-map
+ *     region (cdsp_regions 0x99100000; HakiOS's 0x9c700000 is this phone's splash screen)
+ *
+ * The IPA (mobile data) and going online (DMS/NAS) are left for later: milestone 1 is the modem up,
+ * linked and serving its files, which is all the Wi-Fi needs (modem.md). So no "ipa" SMP2P entry, no
+ * IPA firmware, no DMS/NAS.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg sweetmpss=1 brings the modem up on a thread of its own and leaves it up; sweetmpssstep=N
+ * runs the steps up to N and stops (sweetmpss need not be set then). sweetmpssdelay=S delays the start
+ * (default 20 s, so iOS is up first). modem_keep=1 keeps it up after a limited run. The firmware (77 MB)
+ * is read from /fw/image on the root (iOS/scripts/add-modem-fw.sh puts it there), so the steps wait for
+ * the root to be mounted.
+ *
+ *    1  survey    the shared memory: our partition with the modem, its items, whether it has run
+ *    2  firmware  find and check modem.mdt and its segments on the root; read the modem's file systems
+ *                 (rmtfs) and the service registry's tables (the *.jsn beside the firmware)
+ *    3  header    a modem a kernel before this one left running is stopped; TrustZone takes the image's
+ *                 header (PAS_INIT_IMAGE) and is told where the image will be (PAS_MEM_SETUP)
+ *    4  image     the segments written into the modem's memory, and read back
+ *    5  our item  our SMP2P item (428) made in the partition and filled in; GLINK's marks reset
+ *    6  start     RPMh asked for the rails, the always-on processor told "modem: on", TrustZone asked to
+ *                 authenticate and start the modem (PAS_AUTH_AND_RESET); its first words watched for
+ *    7  link      GLINK taken up (our version, the channel IPCRTR); a thread of ours listens from here;
+ *                 the file services (rmtfs, tftp, the service registry) started
+ *    8  qrtr      the modem's hello answered and the services it tells of listened for (WLFW wanted)
+ *    9  wlfw      the Wi-Fi firmware's service (QMI 0x45), as ath10k: indications, host capabilities, MSA (given by
+ *                 TrustZone to the modem and the WLAN), capabilities, board data, calibration report, "fw ready"
+ *   10  smmu      how the boot chain left apps-smmu for the radio's stream 0x640; with no entry for it, one that lets
+ *                 it through untranslated (bypass, or a free bank with translation off) in a free group
+ *   11  wlan      the copy engines told (pipes, services, shadow registers, as ath10k snoc.c) and the mode MISSION;
+ *                 with sweetwlanread=1 the copy engines' registers read (those of their directions)
+ *   12  htc       the copy engines' rings (CE0-CE3) and read-index page given, receive buffers posted, the
+ *                 firmware's first HTC messages (READY) polled for
+ *   13  wmi       HTC services WMI control and HTT data connected, SETUP COMPLETE, the first WMI events
+ *   14  init      the memory the firmware asked for, WMI INIT (ath10k's resource configuration), READY and the MAC
+ *   15  scan      channel list, a station vdev, a passive scan; the networks heard (beacons) logged
+ *
+ * RPMh is asked for the modem's two rails (step 6) and the Wi-Fi radio's four supplies (step 9), through
+ * sweet_rpmh.c. Nothing writes a clock or a pin; the
+ * SIM is not touched, no call is made, no data session opened.
+ *
+ * Linux: drivers/soc/qcom/{smem,smp2p}.c, drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_*.c, net/qrtr/, qcom_scm; the vendor
+ * subsys-pil-tz.c; github.com/linux-msm/rmtfs and the pd-mapper for the services.
+ */
